---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Image from 'astro/components/Image.astro';
import imgReference_zk from './media/zaveczkrisztina_small.jpg';
---

<Layout pageTitle='Get to know me' pageDescription='A personal website by Krisztina Závecz | Get to know me'>
	<div>
			<p><strong>I'm a Frontend Developer with a love for front-of-the-frontend.</strong></p>
			<section class="intro">
				<p>While working with modern frameworks both at my day-job (React and its ecosystem + TypeScript) and on my side projects (Vue, mostly), the one field that amazes me most is definitely CSS and the way it allows us to ship less JavaScript with each passing day.</p>
			</section>
      <section class="about-me">
        <Image alt="Krisztina Závecz" src={imgReference_zk} width="135" style="transform: rotate(-9deg)" />
        <ul class="likes-list">
          <li><span>I love creating. I find joy in revealing pieces of knowledge I haven't had before.</span></li>
          <li class="bug"><span>I love the feeling of finally resolving a bug. :)</span></li>
          <li><span>I love CSS.</span></li>
					<li><span>I care about accessibility.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section class="tech-current">
				<p><strong>I believe we, as developers, are more than just our current tech stacks.</strong> But if you came here for this:</p>
        <h2 class="small-heading">My current technology stack includes the following technologies:</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Frontend frameworks: React and its ecosystem for my day job, Vue for sideprojects</li>
					<li>Solid foundations in HTML5 - CSS3 - JavaScript / TypeScript</li>
					<li>git / GitHub / GitLab for version control</li>
					<li>Working literacy of modern CI / CD pipelines</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
			<section class="tech-ai">
				<h2 class="small-heading">My current approach with AI:</h2>
				 <p>Besides consciously not outsourcing my thinking to an agent,</p>
				<ul>
					<li>I follow a strict approach: <strong>I never commit code written by AI that I do not understand. </strong> This also implies that I'm always reading the code I commit. I'm working along this approach in my day job, in my side projects and on this personal site.</li>
					<li>I'm not a native English speaker, so I occasionally use LLM-assistance for double-checking certain grammar structures or wording choices. Never feeding it a whole text for re-working or letting it be creative for me.</li>
					<li>You will not see any AI-generated posts on this page.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style lang="stylus" scoped>
	.section
		margin-block: 2em
	.about-me
		border-radius: 6px
		background: #eee
		padding: 6px 12px
		box-shadow: 2px 2px 5px 0px #44618999
		overflow: clip; /* Stylus can't parse this without semi-colons */
		@media screen and (min-width: 400px)
			display: grid
			grid-template-columns: 135px auto
		@media screen and (min-width: 568px)
			align-items: center

	h2.small-heading
		font-size: 1em
		font-family: var(--font-body)
		margin-block: 1em
		color: #444

	.likes-list
		list-style-type: none
		padding-inline-start: 0
		@media screen and (min-width: 568px)
			padding-inline-start: revert

	li
		margin-bottom: 8px

	.likes-list li
		display: flex

	.likes-list span
		align-self: center

	.likes-list li:before
		content: ''
		display: block
		min-width: 30px
		min-height: 30px
		background-image: url("./media/icons8-heart.svg?url")
		background-repeat: no-repeat
		margin-right: 15px

	.likes-list li.bug:before
		background-image: url("./media/FluentEmojiFlatLadyBeetle.svg?url")
		width: 30px
		height: 30px
		transform: rotate(40deg)
</style>